[BlackTeamCountry "ENG"]

1. e4 e6 {Blair normally plays 1...e5, but said he'd had a look at my games
and thought I might be better prepared than him there (doubtful!).} 2. d4 d5 3.
Nd2 dxe4 4. Nxe4 Bd7 5. Nf3 Bc6 6. Bd3 Nd7 {With a tactical draw offer, since
Blair was Black and Battersea outrated us on most boards. I did wonder whether
it was still +EV from a match perspective for me to accept, being heavily
outrated myself, but it felt too negative at such an early stage.} 7. O-O Ngf6
8. Ned2 Be7 9. Re1 Bxf3 10. Nxf3 O-O 11. Bg5 h6 12. Bh4 c5 {This looks close
to equalising, but I managed to keep the tension and retain some pressure for
a while.} 13. c3 Re8 14. Qe2 Qa5 15. a3 cxd4 16. Nxd4 Kf8 {I was surprised by
this move, and the engine doesn't love it. Blair explained after the game that
one of the points is to get out of any Qh7+ tactics, and it might also be
helpful to have the king one square closer to the centre if there are trades
soon.} 17. Bc4 {A drawback of Kf8 is that Nxe6 comes with check, and with Bc4
I prepare some sacrificial ideas. After Blair's accurate reply, none of them
work.} (17. b4 {was another main candidate, with ideas like} Qc7 18. Qxe6 $6 {
, but I thought this looked unimpressive after} Qxc3 {(and I didn't see
anything special after other queen moves on move 17)}) 17... Qh5 18. Qxh5 ({
I probably spent too long here trying to get things like} 18. Qxe6 $4 {to work,
e.g.} fxe6 19. Nxe6+ Kg8 20. Nf4+ {and now if Black is cooperative with e.g.}
Kh8 $4 ({Of course this is all nonsense, and after} 20... Qf7 {Black is
winning.}) 21. Nxh5 Nxh5 22. Rxe7 {White is winning.}) ({The engine suggests} 
18. Nf3 {, which retains a small advantage. This crossed my mind, but going
backwards just to keep pieces on the board isn't really my style.}) 18... Nxh5
19. Bxe7+ Rxe7 20. Rad1 {I felt I might still be a smidge better, but no
longer had realistic winning chances, and was 13 minutes down on the clock, so
offered a draw. The engine says it's 0.0.} 1/2-1/2

